From: =?UTF-8?q?Alexander=20Thei=C3=9Fen?= <alex@theissen.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:04:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] ntdll: Let compatdb keep no-exec permanently on.

Under FEX, a process with data execution prevention off has every
readable page executable, so FEX has to treat all writable memory as
possible code. Each allocation, free or protection change of writable
memory then invalidates translated code, and FEX translates it again.
Wine turns DEP off for a 32-bit process when its executable or a DLL it
loads lacks IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_NX_COMPAT, as many older games do.

When compatdb.so has passed 1 to set_compat_force_nx(), DEP is now
permanently on: ProcessExecuteFlags reports
MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_PERMANENT, and the loader's request to turn DEP off
for a module without the flag fails with STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, with a
warning that says why. SetProcessDEPPolicy(0) never turned DEP off in
Wine, since it passes no flags and gets STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER; with
the lock it gets STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED. Unset (-1) or 0, nothing changes.
compatdb.so runs in start_main_thread() before any PE code, so the value
is in place before the loader maps the main executable and first asks
to turn DEP off.

Wine emulates ATL thunks only in the signal handlers of i386 and x86_64
hosts, and neither wow64 nor FEX does. So a program that runs ATL window
thunks from non-executable heap memory, as the ATL of Visual Studio 2003
does, faults with DEP permanently on; a compatdb rule for such a program
sets the value to 0.

A 64-bit process is not affected: it always reports DEP permanently on.

(cherry picked from commit f1fe4a27b6649a671914f737276cc3d15809468b)
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index ef1ab9602d0..5165d3d7699 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -76,6 +76,15 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(process);
 
 static ULONG execute_flags = MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_DISABLE;
 
+/* When compatdb.so asks for it, no-execute is permanently on: the process
+ * cannot turn it off, whatever its modules say. Otherwise Wine's behavior is
+ * unchanged. */
+static ULONG get_execute_flags(void)
+{
+    if (get_compat_force_nx() == 1) return execute_flags | MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_PERMANENT;
+    return execute_flags;
+}
+
 static UINT process_error_mode;
 ULONG process_cookie = 0xdeadbeef;
 
@@ -1546,7 +1555,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtQueryInformationProcess( HANDLE handle, PROCESSINFOCLASS class
                              MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_DISABLE_THUNK_EMULATION |
                              MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_PERMANENT;
         else
-            *(ULONG *)info = execute_flags;
+            *(ULONG *)info = get_execute_flags();
         break;
 
     case ProcessPriorityClass:
@@ -1871,6 +1880,11 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationProcess( HANDLE handle, PROCESSINFOCLASS class,
     case ProcessExecuteFlags:
         if ((is_win64 && !is_wow64()) || size != sizeof(ULONG)) return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
         if (execute_flags & MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_PERMANENT) return STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
+        if (get_execute_flags() & MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_PERMANENT)
+        {
+            WARN( "no-exec stays on because compatdb.so keeps it permanently on\n" );
+            return STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
+        }
         else
         {
             BOOL enable;
